  "bookName": "Romans",
  "bookOrder": 45,
  "testament": "new",
  "chapter": 14,
  "sortOrder": 45014,
  "verseCount": 23,
  "aliases": [
    "Rom",
    "Ro",
    "Rm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Him that is weak in the faith receive ye, but not to doubtful disputations.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "For one believeth that he may eat all things: another, who is weak, eateth herbs.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Let not him that eateth despise him that eateth not; and let not him which eateth not judge him that eateth: for God hath received him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Who art thou that judgest another man’s servant? to his own master he standeth or falleth. Yea, he shall be holden up: for God is able to make him stand.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "One man esteemeth one day above another: another esteemeth every day alike. Let every man be fully persuaded in his own mind.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "He that regardeth the day, regardeth it unto the Lord; and he that regardeth not the day, to the Lord he doth not regard it. He that eateth, eateth to the Lord, for he giveth God thanks; and he that eateth not, to the Lord he eateth not, and giveth God thanks.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "For none of us liveth to himself, and no man dieth to himself.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "For whether we live, we live unto the Lord; and whether we die, we die unto the Lord: whether we live therefore, or die, we are the Lord’s.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "For to this end Christ both died, and rose, and revived, that he might be Lord both of the dead and living.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "But why dost thou judge thy brother? or why dost thou set at nought thy brother? for we shall all stand before the judgment seat of Christ.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "For it is written, As I live, saith the Lord, every knee shall bow to me, and every tongue shall confess to God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "So then every one of us shall give account of himself to God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Let us not therefore judge one another any more: but judge this rather, that no man put a stumblingblock or an occasion to fall in his brother’s way.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "I know, and am persuaded by the Lord Jesus, that there is nothing unclean of itself: but to him that esteemeth any thing to be unclean, to him it is unclean.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "But if thy brother be grieved with thy meat, now walkest thou not charitably. Destroy not him with thy meat, for whom Christ died.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Let not then your good be evil spoken of:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "For the kingdom of God is not meat and drink; but righteousness, and peace, and joy in the Holy Ghost.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "For he that in these things serveth Christ is acceptable to God, and approved of men.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Let us therefore follow after the things which make for peace, and things wherewith one may edify another.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "For meat destroy not the work of God. All things indeed are pure; but it is evil for that man who eateth with offence.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "It is good neither to eat flesh, nor to drink wine, nor any thing whereby thy brother stumbleth, or is offended, or is made weak.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Hast thou faith? have it to thyself before God. Happy is he that condemneth not himself in that thing which he alloweth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:14:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "And he that doubteth is damned if he eat, because he eateth not of faith: for whatsoever is not of faith is sin.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 14:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:14:23"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
